{
  "moduleId": "packages-chord",
  "name": "Packages Chord",
  "generatedAt": "2026-09-23T15:14:09.039Z",
  "summary": "Chord is the structural module for packages/chord, implementing a facet-based application architecture. It provides a delta-based state tracking system for JSON data, a dependency-injected service framework with local and remote instances, facet lifecycle management, bundling/loading of facet bundles for Node.js, and serialization/validation of service wire protocol messages. Includes an immutable delta application API, reactive subscriptions with context propagation for cancellation, and node-specific tooling to package facets into distributable bundles with integrity manifests.",
  "keyPoints": [
    "Provides delta-based state tracking: `track` observes mutations on JSON objects via proxies and emits compact operation lists (replace/set/delete/append/transform/patch) for efficient replication; `apply` applies ops to a target, `applyImmutable` creates new instances, and string diffs use suffix detection with configurable overlap scanning.",
    "Facet lifecycle: `createFacetHost` in api.ts manages facets through states (setting_up → prepared → active → disposing → dead), topological ordering of dependencies, staged service activation, reload support detecting shape/reference changes, and disposal of owned resources.",
    "Remote services: `RemoteServiceProvider` (provider.ts) classifies implementations into methods and replicated state members, validates them against RemoteServiceContract for JSON-compatible types, and supports singleton and keyed service instances with generation-based addresses, replacement (replacing implementations), spawning (creating keyed instances), subscriptions for state updates, and withdrawal.",
    "Service wire encoding: `encoder`/`decoder` in delta/index.ts convert internal Ops to compact WireOps omitting implied paths during subscriptions; service-wire.ts defines wire snapshot/update formats with control calls (catalogue/subscribe/unsubscribe) and strict parsing/validation for cross-process communication.",
    "Node bundling: `bundleFacets` (node/bundle.ts) uses esbuild to compile facet sources into a chord.facet-bundle format (version 2) with manifest chord-facets.json; `createFacetBundleLoader` loads and executes such bundles, resolving external imports via resolver or node require, verifying integrity hashes, and materializing artifact files.",
    "Context system: context/index.ts provides immutable ContextKey/Context with BackgroundContext and TODO, value scoping, abort signal propagation/cancellation, and `awaitWithContext` to track pending operations; built-in ABORT_SIGNAL_CONTEXT_KEY integrates with cancellation flows."
  ],
  "entryPoints": [
    {
      "name": "track",
      "file": "src/delta/index.ts",
      "note": "Creates a Tracker wrapping a JSON object; mutations made through the returned proxy are recorded as delta Ops accessible via flush/rebase/discard. Used as the core change-tracking mechanism for replicated state."
    },
    {
      "name": "apply",
      "file": "src/delta/index.ts",
      "note": "Applies an array of Ops to a target object, mutating it in place; supports all op types and validates path safety/index ranges."
    },
    {
      "name": "applyImmutable",
      "file": "src/delta/index.ts",
      "note": "Applies Ops without mutating the input; copies containers along changed paths and returns a new object structure (for immutable state management)."
    },
    {
      "name": "createFacetHost",
      "file": "src/api.ts",
      "note": "Async factory creating a FacetHost that manages facet lifecycles, service provision, and reloading; the main entry point for running facets."
    },
    {
      "name": "defineService",
      "file": "src/api.ts",
      "note": "Defines a Service with an ID and optional local-only flag; used to declare service contracts consumed/provided across facets and remote hosts."
    },
    {
      "name": "createRemoteServiceBinding",
      "file": "src/api.ts",
      "note": "Creates a RemoteServiceBinding that connects to a remote service provider via a transport, enabling use/observe of remote services with hydration and rebind support."
    },
    {
      "name": "bundleFacets",
      "file": "src/node/bundle.ts",
      "note": "Node-specific bundling of facet sources into distributable bundle artifacts with manifest and integrity checks; primary tool for packaging facets for deployment."
    },
    {
      "name": "createFacetBundleLoader",
      "file": "src/node/bundle-loader.ts",
      "note": "Creates a FacetLoader that loads a bundled facet artifact from disk, verifying manifest integrity and executing the bundle to extract facet definitions."
    },
    {
      "name": "RemoteServiceProvider",
      "file": "src/services/provider.ts",
      "note": "Central class for providing remote services; provide/withdraw/replace/spawn manage service implementations, and invoke/subscribe handle calls and state updates for bound clients."
    },
    {
      "name": "createLoopbackServiceTransport",
      "file": "src/services/loopback.ts",
      "note": "Creates a RemoteServiceTransport that routes calls/subscriptions directly to a given RemoteServiceProvider within the same process, used for testing and local facades."
    }
  ],
